schema: "0.4"
id: workbench-09-graded-projects
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns (a CLI learning tool) — Graded Projects: a hands-on project graded by the sub-agent against a rubric. HERO screen.
# Theme tenets: warm cream "maker's reference sheet" on a cork board inside a terminal window; a big handwritten grade + a stack of pinned rubric cards + a taped citation list joined by a hand-drawn arrow; printed labels + marker titles + mono; 3px cut-paper radius; clay accents.
# Palette: cream #f5f0e8, brown ink #2c2416, cork #c4a574, marker blue #2980b9, clay orange #e67e22, marker red #e74c3c, marker green #27ae60, sticky yellow #fef3b5, tan #d4c9b5.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity, identity-defining
    HERO mockup of a command-line learning tool's GRADED PROJECTS surface, skinned
    as a warm cream "maker's reference sheet" pinned to a cork board inside a
    terminal window — a hands-on project just graded by a sub-agent against a
    rubric. Tactile, informal, encouraging: a big handwritten grade, pinned rubric
    index cards, a taped citation list, hand-drawn arrows. This is the maker's-bench
    voice at its fullest — pen, tape and pushpins on warm paper, the inverse of a
    dark chalkboard. It is a text-mode tool window, never a web browser page.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity HERO mockup of a single TERMINAL WINDOW showing the GRADED
    PROJECTS surface of "The Robot Learns", a command-line learning tool. The
    content pane is skinned as a warm cream MAKER'S REFERENCE SHEET pinned to a
    subtle CORK BOARD — note cards, masking tape and pushpins. Fill the frame with
    ONE tool window and a thin top title bar; NO web browser chrome, no tabs, no
    address bar.

    TITLE BAR (thin, top): a warm cream bar with three small window dots and, in
    fixed-width type, "learn project --grade · build-a-cache".

    HERO — THE GRADE (top-left, dominant): a large pinned "graded" note card lifted
    well off the board by a soft warm-brown shadow, a red pushpin at its corner, a
    BIG handwritten marker grade "B+" beside a marker-green tick, and a printed
    sub-line "Build a write-through cache · matched to your level".

    RUBRIC FEEDBACK (center, a stack of pinned index cards): three overlapping
    PINNED CARDS, each a per-criterion evaluation — a handwritten marker criterion
    title ("Correctness", "Concurrency safety", "Tests") with a small marker tick or
    cross, and two printed feedback lines underneath. One card is tilted a degree;
    each has its own pushpin. Correctness earns a green tick, Concurrency safety a
    marker-red cross with a "race on eviction" note.

    CITATIONS (right, taped strip): a masking-taped list titled in marker "see also",
    with monospace KB references ("kb/caching/write-through.md",
    "kb/concurrency/locks.md"), a pushpin at the top. A loose HAND-DRAWN ARROW curls
    from the Concurrency-safety rubric card over to the "locks.md" citation.

    BOTTOM STATUS RULE: a persistent thin bar with fixed-width keybind hints
    "^R resubmit   ^O open citation   ^N next project   ^Q quit".

    PALETTE & TYPE: warm cream paper on a muted cork board, brown-ink text; friendly
    clay accents — marker blue for headings and the connector arrow, clay orange for
    tape and accent borders, marker red for the failing cross and pushpins, marker
    green for the passing ticks and the grade. Handwritten marker script for the
    grade, criterion titles, arrows and margin notes; a clean printed geometric sans
    for feedback and labels; fixed-width monospace for the citation paths.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: barely-rounded cut-paper corners; cards lifted off the cork by
    soft warm-brown drop shadows (deliberate elevation, two steps for the hero
    grade); slight rotations; separation by air, tape and shadow, never ruled boxes;
    sanctioned cork and paper grain that never hurts legibility.

    MOOD: a proud, encouraging maker's bench the morning after a build — organized
    chaos that makes sense, warm and hands-on, pen-and-tape on cream paper; the
    light maker-bench inverse of a dark slate chalkboard.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, web browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, marketing web page, sterile flat corporate report card, dark terminal background, dark chalkboard slate, monochrome CRT"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Reads as a graded-projects surface skinned as a maker's cream sheet on cork: a dominant pinned grade card (big handwritten grade + green tick + project sub-line), a stack of pinned per-criterion rubric feedback cards with ticks/crosses and short feedback, and a taped citation list of monospace KB references joined to a rubric card by a hand-drawn arrow; title bar; bottom keybind status rule"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Warm cream paper on cork + brown ink with clay accents; handwritten marker grade/titles/arrows + printed sans feedback + monospace citations; pinned cards with soft warm shadows, tape, pushpins, slight rotation; cut-paper radius; light maker-bench not dark chalkboard"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Strong hero hierarchy with the grade dominant, legible rubric stack and citation strip, plausible real tool window"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "web browser chrome or a marketing web page instead of a tool window"
    - "dark terminal, dark chalkboard, or monochrome CRT instead of warm cream paper skin"

tags: [workbench, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, hero]
